      ],
      "calibration": "This is a procedural appeal lever: if the exam was inadequate, it may entitle the veteran to a new examination. The corpus does not directly address examination adequacy standards, but § 3.310 presupposes that causation has been fairly investigated. This theory requires analyzing the examination record itself."
